§§ `Part 6: unfair dismissal`

`p6 yes` MEANS `yes: Part 6 (unfair dismissal) applies to your dismissal`
`p6 high earner` MEANS `no: Part 6 does not apply to a non-award employee whose remuneration immediately before the dismissal was at or above the indexed threshold a year (s 105A(1)(a))`

#ASSERT `Does Part 6 apply to my dismissal` TRUE FALSE FALSE 100321 100322 FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `p6 yes`
#ASSERT `Does Part 6 apply to my dismissal` TRUE FALSE FALSE 100322 100322 FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `p6 high earner`
#ASSERT `Does Part 6 apply to my dismissal` TRUE FALSE TRUE 150000 100322 FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `p6 yes`
#ASSERT `Does Part 6 apply to my dismissal` TRUE TRUE TRUE 50000 100322 FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `no: Part 6 does not apply to an apprentice; an apprentice may apply to SAET under the South Australian Skills Act 2008 (s 105A(1)(b))`
#ASSERT `Does Part 6 apply to my dismissal` TRUE FALSE TRUE 50000 100322 TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `no: Part 6 does not apply to the end of a contract for a specified period or task at its end, unless the employer's conduct gave you a clear expectation of continuing employment (s 105A(4))`
#ASSERT `Does Part 6 apply to my dismissal` TRUE FALSE TRUE 50000 100322 TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `p6 yes`
#ASSERT `Does Part 6 apply to my dismissal` TRUE FALSE TRUE 50000 100322 FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `no: the regulations exclude you from Part 6 (s 105A(2))`
#ASSERT `Does Part 6 apply to my dismissal` FALSE FALSE TRUE 50000 100322 FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `no: Part 6 applies only to an employee under this Act whose employment the Act covers (ss 4, 6)`

`ud in time` MEANS `in time: you applied before the end of 21 days from the date the dismissal took effect; no fee may be charged (s 106(1), (4))`
`ud late` MEANS `out of time: you did not apply before the end of 21 days from the date the dismissal took effect (s 106(1)); Part 6 gives no power to extend the time (whether the South Australian Employment Tribunal Act 2014 does is outside this encoding)`

