§§ `ss 115, 116B, 223, 233, 235(2)`

`pr yes` MEANS `yes: it is an offence for an employer to do this for a prohibited reason, maximum penalty $20 000 (s 115, s 116B(1)); once the employer is convicted you may apply to that court for compensation for your loss and, if you were dismissed, re-employment (s 116B(2)); a prosecution must be commenced within 2 years (s 235(2))`
`absent` MEANS `(m) I was absent from work without leave`
`m no` MEANS `no: absence without leave is a prohibited reason only if the absence was to carry out duties or exercise rights as an officer of an association, and you applied for leave beforehand and it was unreasonably refused or withheld (s 115(m))`

#ASSERT `Was it done for a prohibited reason` `dismissed me, or threatened to` `(a) I am, have been or propose to become an officer, delegate or member of an association` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `pr yes`
#ASSERT `Was it done for a prohibited reason` `refused to employ me, or threatened to` `(b) I am not, or do not propose to become, a member of an association` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `pr yes`
#ASSERT `Was it done for a prohibited reason` `altered my position to my prejudice, or threatened to` `(i) I made or proposed an inquiry or complaint to a body able to seek compliance with industrial law or enforcement of my rights` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `pr yes`
#ASSERT `Was it done for a prohibited reason` `something else the employer did` `(a) I am, have been or propose to become an officer, delegate or member of an association` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `not covered: s 116B(1) lists only dismissal, injury in employment, prejudicial alteration of position, refusal to employ and discriminatory terms of an offer, done or threatened`
#ASSERT `Was it done for a prohibited reason` `dismissed me, or threatened to` `none of these` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `no: the employer did not act for a prohibited reason; the reasons are listed in s 115`
#ASSERT `Was it done for a prohibited reason` `dismissed me, or threatened to` `absent` TRUE TRUE EQUALS `pr yes`
#ASSERT `Was it done for a prohibited reason` `dismissed me, or threatened to` `absent` TRUE FALSE EQUALS `m no`
#ASSERT `Was it done for a prohibited reason` `dismissed me, or threatened to` `absent` FALSE TRUE EQUALS `m no`

`ip yes` MEANS `yes: it is an offence (s 223(1)), maximum penalty $20 000; you may commence the prosecution yourself (s 223(3)) within 2 years (s 235(2)); once the employer is convicted you may apply for compensation for your loss and, if you were dismissed, re-employment (s 223(4))`

#ASSERT `Was it done because I took part in industrial proceedings` `dismissed me` `(a) my participation in proceedings before SAET` FALSE EQUALS `ip yes`
#ASSERT `Was it done because I took part in industrial proceedings` `threatened to prejudice me in my employment` `(c) my participation in an industrial dispute` FALSE EQUALS `ip yes`
#ASSERT `Was it done because I took part in industrial proceedings` `dismissed me` `(a) my participation in proceedings before SAET` TRUE EQUALS `no: discrimination on the ground that you contravened a determination of SAET or committed an offence is not made unlawful by s 223(1) (s 223(2))`
#ASSERT `Was it done because I took part in industrial proceedings` `something else done to me` `(a) my participation in proceedings before SAET` FALSE EQUALS `not covered: s 223(1) reaches only dismissal or prejudice in employment, done or threatened`
#ASSERT `Was it done because I took part in industrial proceedings` `dismissed me` `another reason` FALSE EQUALS `not covered: s 223(1) reaches only the reasons it lists (SAET proceedings, an industrial dispute, an award or enterprise agreement)`

`pros in time` MEANS `in time: the prosecution was commenced within 2 years after the date of the alleged offence (s 235(2))`
`pros late` MEANS `out of time: a prosecution must be commenced within 2 years after the date of the alleged offence (s 235(2))`

#ASSERT `Is the prosecution in time` (dmy 10 4 2026) (dmy 10 4 2028) EQUALS `pros in time`
#ASSERT `Is the prosecution in time` (dmy 10 4 2026) (dmy 11 4 2028) EQUALS `pros late`
#ASSERT `Is the prosecution in time` (dmy 29 2 2028) (dmy 28 2 2030) EQUALS `pros in time`
#ASSERT `Is the prosecution in time` (dmy 29 2 2028) (dmy 1 3 2030) EQUALS `pros late`
#ASSERT `Is the prosecution in time` (dmy 10 4 2026) (dmy 9 4 2026) EQUALS `too early: the alleged offence date is after the date the prosecution was commenced`

#ASSERT `What can I apply for after the conviction` `s 116B, dismissal or other action for a prohibited reason` TRUE EQUALS `you may apply to the convicting court for compensation for loss resulting from the offence and an order that the employer re-employ you on conditions the court determines (s 116B(2)); and for an order to pay any amount the employer owes you (s 233)`
#ASSERT `What can I apply for after the conviction` `s 116B, dismissal or other action for a prohibited reason` FALSE EQUALS `you may apply to the convicting court for compensation for loss resulting from the offence (s 116B(2)(a)); and for an order to pay any amount the employer owes you (s 233)`
#ASSERT `What can I apply for after the conviction` `s 223, discrimination for taking part in industrial proceedings` TRUE EQUALS `you may apply to the convicting court for compensation for loss resulting from the offence and an order that the employer re-employ you on conditions the court determines (s 223(4)); and for an order to pay any amount the employer owes you (s 233)`
#ASSERT `What can I apply for after the conviction` `s 223, discrimination for taking part in industrial proceedings` FALSE EQUALS `you may apply to the convicting court for compensation for loss resulting from the offence (s 223(4)(a)); and for an order to pay any amount the employer owes you (s 233)`
#ASSERT `What can I apply for after the conviction` `another offence against this Act committed in respect of me` TRUE EQUALS `you may apply to the convicting court for an order that the employer pay you an amount it owes you; an inspector's certificate proves the amount unless the contrary is proved (s 233)`
